<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Native token practice · Full stack and lifetime evidence</title>
<style>
:root{--ink:#172f35;--muted:#627579;--paper:#f4f6f3;--line:#dce4df;--green:#087466;--orange:#965217;--red:#a33435}
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:15px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}header{background:var(--ink);color:white;padding:19px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1280px)/2));display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:20px}header span{font:12px monospace;letter-spacing:1.7px}header button{background:transparent;color:white;border:1px solid #59716f}main{max-width:1330px;margin:auto;padding:40px 24px 70px}h1{font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,56px);line-height:1.1;margin:10px 0 18px;letter-spacing:-1.8px}h2{font-size:27px;line-height:1.2;margin:28px 0 16px}h3{font-size:18px;margin:0 0 9px}p{margin:10px 0 15px}a{color:var(--green);overflow-wrap:anywhere;text-underline-offset:3px}.eyebrow{font:12px monospace;letter-spacing:1.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--green)}.lede{max-width:950px;font-size:18px}.muted,.small{color:var(--muted)}.small{font-size:12px}.stamp{font:12px monospace;color:var(--muted);overflow-wrap:anywhere}button,input,select{font:inherit}button{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:9px 15px;border-radius:7px;cursor:pointer;background:white;color:var(--ink)}nav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:9;background:var(--paper);display:flex;gap:8px;overflow:auto;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin:16px 0 25px}nav button{white-space:nowrap}nav button[aria-selected=true]{background:var(--ink);border-color:var(--ink);color:white}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:15px}.card,.box{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:22px;min-width:0}.card strong.metric{display:block;font-size:31px;line-height:1.2;margin:12px 0 9px;letter-spacing:-1px}.pill{display:inline-block;font-size:11px;font-weight:650;padding:4px 8px;border-radius:20px;background:#e6f2ec;color:var(--green);margin:2px 3px 2px 0}.warn{background:#fff1df;color:var(--orange)}.bad{background:#fae4e4;color:var(--red)}.note{padding:16px 20px;border-left:3px solid var(--green);background:#e7f2ed;margin:22px 0}.note.warn{border-color:var(--orange);background:#fff3e2}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}.table-wrap{overflow:auto;background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}th{text-align:left;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;color:var(--muted);background:#edf1ed;white-space:nowrap}td,th{padding:15px 17px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}td{max-width:530px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}tr:last-child td{border-bottom:0}code{font:12px ui-monospace,monospace;overflow-wrap:anywhere}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;overflow:auto;max-height:390px;background:#edf3f0;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:15px;border-radius:8px;font:12px/1.55 ui-monospace,monospace;color:#244a48}details{margin:8px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;color:var(--green);overflow-wrap:anywhere}details.native{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:16px;margin:10px 0}.toolbar{display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;margin:16px 0;flex-wrap:wrap}input{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:11px 14px;border-radius:7px;min-width:250px;flex:1}.empty{padding:25px;color:var(--muted)}.positive{color:var(--green)}.negative{color:var(--red)}footer{padding-top:30px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}[hidden]{display:none!important}
@media(max-width:900px){.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:600px){main{padding:28px 16px 50px}header{padding:15px 16px}.grid,.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.card{padding:18px}.card strong.metric{font-size:29px}nav{padding:12px 0}td,th{padding:12px}.toolbar input{min-width:100%}h1{letter-spacing:-1px}}@media print{nav,button,input{display:none}.panel[hidden]{display:block!important}.table-wrap,pre{overflow:visible;max-height:none}header{background:white;color:black}.cards{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}}
</style></head><body><header><span>NATIVE STACK / MEASURED PRACTICE</span><button id="export">Export full JSON</button></header><main>
<div class="eyebrow">PC-wide evidence · Native commands</div><h1>The full stack.<br>Results you can trace.</h1><p class="lede">TOON, Context Mode, RTK, Headroom and the complete selected stack. Native reports are captured directly; lifetime estimates, exact output measurements and provider trials retain their own scope.</p><p class="stamp" id="stamp"></p>
<nav aria-label="Manifest views"><button data-tab="overview" aria-selected="true">Savings overview</button><button data-tab="native">Native returned results</button><button data-tab="adoption">Adoption & hooks</button><button data-tab="tools">All tools</button><button data-tab="catalog">Grand catalogs</button><button data-tab="evidence">E2E evidence</button><button data-tab="practice">Future sessions & PC</button></nav>
<section class="panel" id="overview"><div id="dollar-explanation" class="box"></div><h2>Native counters and their actual boundaries</h2><div id="native-cards" class="cards"></div><div class="note"><strong>No combined “tokens saved” total.</strong> Native cumulative counters overlap their project/session views. Artifact reductions compare retained text; provider trials measure actual session consumption. Exact full-PC lifetime provider savings is unavailable.</div>
<h2>Persistent native history</h2><p>The local ledger preserves observed native events and snapshots across sessions. These are retained records from known dates, not a reconstruction of unrecorded PC history.</p><div id="event-table"></div>
<h2>TOON: current grand catalog, direct upstream conversion</h2><div id="toon-summary" class="box"></div>
<h2>Matched native agent trials</h2><div id="provider-cards" class="grid"></div>
<h2>Additional native research baselines</h2><div id="research-baselines"></div><h2>Retrieval quality baseline</h2><div id="retrieval-baseline" class="box"></div>
<h2>Coverage and resolved gaps</h2><div id="coverage-summary"></div></section>
<section class="panel" id="native" hidden><div id="current-native-results"></div><h2>The returned upstream reports</h2><p>Every block below retains the complete returned text. Native JSON files are identified separately from CLI/MCP invocations. Commands, timestamps and raw evidence remain available.</p><div id="native-results"></div></section>
<section class="panel" id="adoption" hidden><h2>Native adoption and observed hooks</h2><p>Enabled configuration, recorded hook events and completed tasks are separate evidence. The table reads only the three configured client homes. It does not infer adoption in every catalog repository.</p><div id="hook-inventory"></div><h2>Recorded savings by working directory</h2><p>These rows partition the native RTK history by its stored working-directory field. Validation fixtures remain visible. Native project commands are rerun wherever that original directory still exists; deleted directories retain database evidence only.</p><div id="project-counters"></div><h2>Coverage of the entire catalog</h2><div id="adoption-totals"></div><p>Unmeasured is not zero. Research inclusion, an installed command, functional acceptance, a token baseline and a causal lifetime saving are different claims.</p></section>
<section class="panel" id="tools" hidden><h2>All selected stack components</h2><p id="tools-intro"></p><div class="toolbar"><input id="tool-search" type="search" placeholder="Find TOON, Context Mode, retrieval, browser…" aria-label="Search all tools"><span id="tool-count" class="small"></span></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Repository / installed pin</th><th>Adoption / latest check</th><th>Native lifetime command / returned value</th><th>Baseline / quality</th><th>Hook / adoption lane</th></tr></thead><tbody id="tool-rows"></tbody></table></div><h2>Supporting runtimes and other installations</h2><p>Support runtimes and optional/older installation records stay separate from the selected component count. A directory or version probe alone does not establish active use or E2E acceptance.</p><div id="support-runtimes"></div></section>
<section class="panel" id="catalog" hidden><h2>Grand repository catalog</h2><p id="catalog-summary"></p><div class="toolbar"><input id="catalog-search" type="search" placeholder="Search every repository, source or decision…" aria-label="Search grand catalog"><span id="catalog-count" class="small"></span></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Repository</th><th>Recorded coverage</th><th>Source decisions and references</th></tr></thead><tbody id="catalog-rows"></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="panel" id="evidence" hidden><h2>Exact retained-output comparisons</h2><p>Named tokenizer: <strong>gpt-tokenizer 3.4.0 / o200k_base</strong>. Each input/output pair is retained and hash-checked. Re-importing an identical pair does not increase the count. These are unique evidenced transformations, not actual-use or lifetime provider counters.</p><div id="comparison-table"></div><details class="box"><summary>All seven Headroom guarded offline fixtures</summary><div id="headroom-fixtures"></div></details><h2>Every captured E2E operation</h2><p>Full commands and returned output from the original audit and fresh gap repairs. Functional checks, current-state queries, native task trials and historical evidence remain distinct.</p><div class="toolbar"><input id="operation-search" type="search" placeholder="Filter command, component or result…" aria-label="Search captured operations"><span id="operation-count" class="small"></span></div><div id="operation-results"></div><h2>Provider commands and raw accounting</h2><div id="provider-evidence"></div></section>
<section class="panel" id="practice" hidden><h2>Installed for future sessions</h2><div id="practice-content"></div><h2>GitHub and grand-catalog practice</h2><p>The public practice, adoption entry points and sanitized receipts are maintained in the publication repository. Private command output, personal paths and native session transcripts stay local. Use the canonical catalog generator and offline validators before integrating a catalog change.</p><pre>python3 scripts/catalog_decisions.py --write
python3 scripts/catalog_decisions.py --check
python3 scripts/validate.py
python3 scripts/validate_catalogs.py</pre><p id="public-links"></p><details class="box"><summary>Local configuration and source identities</summary><div id="config-details"></div></details></section>
<footer>Single-file local HTML. No remote scripts, analytics, model calls or service actions are performed by this page. Live source files may change after capture; retained raw files and hashes identify the observed results.</footer>
</main><script id="data" type="application/json">__DATA__</script><script>
"use strict";const D=JSON.parse(document.getElementById("data").textContent),$=id=>document.getElementById(id);
const e=v=>String(v??"").replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({"&":"&amp;","<":"&lt;",">":"&gt;",'"':"&quot;","'":"&#39;"}[c]));
const n=v=>typeof v==="number"?v.toLocaleString("en-US"):"Unavailable";
const pre=v=>"<pre>"+e(typeof v==="string"?v:JSON.stringify(v,null,2))+"</pre>";
function localHref(path,base=location.href){const url=new URL(base);if(path.startsWith('/')&&!path.startsWith('//')&&url.protocol==='file:'){if(['wsl$','wsl.localhost'].includes(url.hostname.toLowerCase())){const distribution=url.pathname.split('/')[1];return new URL('/'+distribution+path,url).href;}return new URL(path,url).href;}return path;}
const a=(p,l)=>{if(!/^(https?:\/\/|\/)/.test(p||""))return e(l||p);if(p.startsWith('/')&&location.protocol!=='file:'){const root=D.configuration.publication;if(root&&p.startsWith(root+'/')){const relative=p.slice(root.length+1).split('/').map(encodeURIComponent).join('/');return '<a href="https://github.com/seathatflowsinourveins/native-agent-stack/blob/main/'+e(relative)+'">'+e(l||p)+'</a>';}return '<span title="Retained local file; not served by this HTTP page. Use the attached download when available.">'+e(l||p)+' <small>(local file)</small></span>';}return '<a href="'+e(localHref(p))+'">'+e(l||p)+'</a>';};
const pill=(s,bad=false)=>'<span class="pill '+(bad?"warn":"")+'">'+e(s)+"</span>";
const roots=D.configuration,ops=[...(D.audit.operations||[]),...(D.gaps?.operations||[]),...(D.additional_evidence?.fresh_e2e?.result?.operations||[])];
const coverage=D.stack.components.map(c=>{const old=D.audit.coverage.find(x=>x.id===c.id)||{};const gap=D.gaps?.components?.find(x=>x.id===c.id)||{};return {...old,...c,...gap};});
const rows=D.catalog.records||[];
const matrix=D.coverage_matrix||[],repoMatrix=D.repository_coverage||[],extra=D.additional_evidence||{};
function showTab(id){for(const x of document.querySelectorAll(".panel"))x.hidden=x.id!==id;for(const b of document.querySelectorAll("nav button"))b.setAttribute("aria-selected",String(b.dataset.tab===id));history.replaceState(null,"","#"+id);window.scrollTo(0,0);}
document.querySelectorAll("nav button").forEach(b=>b.onclick=()=>showTab(b.dataset.tab));
function good(tool,scope){return D.native.find(v=>v.tool===tool&&(!scope||v.scope.includes(scope)))?.latest_success;}
const rtk=good("rtk","all retained"),cm=good("context-mode","Desktop"),headroom=good("headroom");
$("stamp").textContent="Captured "+D.generated_at+" · "+rows.length+" catalog identities · "+coverage.length+" selected components · "+D.comparisons.length+" unique exact-output comparisons";
function card(title,value,scope,note){return '<article class="card"><div class="eyebrow">'+e(title)+'</div><strong class="metric">'+e(value)+'</strong><div>'+e(scope)+'</div><p class="small">'+e(note)+"</p></article>";}
const money=D.dollar_explanation||{};
$("dollar-explanation").innerHTML='<div class="eyebrow">Why the quoted $0.65 / $0.85 is small</div><h2>“Lifetime” belongs to a retained data store.</h2><p>'+e(money.why_small)+'</p><p><strong>Latest returned dollar line: '+e(money.current_footer||money.current_dollar_line||"No dollar line in this report")+'</strong><br><span class="small">'+e(money.current_runtime)+' · '+e(money.captured_at)+'</span></p><p>'+e(money.retention)+'</p><p class="small">The earlier quotation has no captured runtime identity. The quotation alone cannot identify a whole-PC lifetime or be assigned to one client.</p><details><summary>Exact upstream formulas and dollar assumptions</summary>'+pre(money)+'</details>';
$("native-cards").innerHTML=card("RTK",rtk?n(rtk.metrics.saved):"Unavailable","estimated tokens · retained history","Native gain result. 90-day configured retention; all projects includes this project's subset.")+card("Context Mode",cm?n(cm.metrics.saved):"Unavailable","native lifetime event estimate","Latest persisted Desktop runtime file. Retained events ×256; session bytes use a different estimate.")+card("Headroom",headroom?n(headroom.metrics.saved):"Unavailable","recorded native savings · 30 days","Its native lifetime field is capped at30days. Zero here means no native ledger events; offline guard evidence is separate.")+card("TOON","Per conversion","no upstream lifetime counter","Direct --stats output plus exact tokenizer comparison. Durable local evidence records start from captured inputs.");
$("event-table").innerHTML=D.preserved_native_events.length?'<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Native history</th><th>Recorded events</th><th>Estimated tokens saved</th><th>Known interval</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+D.preserved_native_events.map(x=>"<tr><td>"+e(x.tool)+"<br>"+e(x.scope)+"</td><td>"+n(x.events)+"</td><td>"+n(x.estimated_saved)+"</td><td>"+e(x.first_event)+"<br>"+e(x.last_event)+"</td></tr>").join("")+"</tbody></table></div>":'<p class="empty">No native events have been archived yet.</p>';
$("toon-summary").innerHTML=D.toon.roundtrip_exact?"<h3>"+n(D.toon.baseline.tokens)+" → "+n(D.toon.candidate.tokens)+" exact output tokens</h3><p><strong>"+n(Math.abs(D.toon.tokens_removed))+" "+(D.toon.tokens_removed>=0?"fewer":"more")+"</strong> versus the complete compact JSON catalog. Strict semantic roundtrip passed. Selected format: "+e(D.toon.selected_format)+".</p><p class=\"small\">Original formatted JSON: "+n(D.toon.original?.tokens)+" tokens. The upstream --stats heuristic uses its own JSON formatting/token estimate; that different baseline can report a saving while compact JSON is smaller.</p><p>"+a(D.toon.baseline.path,"Complete compact JSON")+" · "+a(D.toon.candidate.path,"Direct upstream TOON output")+"</p>":pre(D.toon);
$("provider-cards").innerHTML=D.audit.provider_pairs.map(p=>'<div class="card"><div class="eyebrow">'+e(p.client)+" · "+e(p.model)+'</div><h3 class="'+(p.observed_tokens_fewer>=0?"positive":"negative")+'">'+n(Math.abs(p.observed_tokens_fewer))+" "+(p.observed_tokens_fewer>=0?"fewer":"more")+' tokens</h3><p>'+n(p.baseline_total)+" → "+n(p.candidate_total)+". Both task variants passed.</p><p class=\"small\">One fixed-order Context Mode non-use / explicit-use pair. Cache warmth and full plugin absence were not controlled. Coordinator/report costs excluded.</p></div>").join("");
function table(headers,body){return '<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr>'+headers.map(h=>'<th>'+e(h)+'</th>').join('')+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+body+'</tbody></table></div>';}
const study=extra.native_study?.result;
const installation=extra.native_installation?.result,acceptance=extra.native_client_acceptance?.result;
if(installation){
  const profiles=installation.profiles||[],runs=acceptance?.runs||[],aggregate=acceptance?.aggregate_acceptance||[];
  const checks=value=>Object.entries(value||{}).map(([key,passed])=>pill(key.replaceAll('_',' ')+': '+(passed===true?'passed':passed===false?'failed':String(passed)),passed!==true)).join(' ');
  const installed=table(['Client','Installed upstream awareness','Observed checks'],profiles.map(p=>'<tr><td><strong>'+e(p.client)+'</strong></td><td>'+a(p.awareness.path,'RTK instructions')+'<br>'+a(p.instructions.path,'Startup instructions')+'<details><summary>Upstream command and complete returned result</summary>'+pre(p.command.argv)+pre(p.command.stdout_text)+pre(p.command.stderr_text)+'</details></td><td>'+checks(p.checks)+'</td></tr>').join(''));
  const clients=runs.length?table(['Fresh native task','Actual checks','Returned usage / evidence'],runs.map(r=>'<tr><td><strong>'+e(r.client)+' · '+e(r.attempt||'recorded')+'</strong><p>'+pill(r.passed?'Task accepted':'Gap retained',!r.passed)+'</p></td><td>'+checks(r.checks)+(r.failures?.length?pre(r.failures):'')+'</td><td>'+pre(r.usage)+'<p class="small">Actual task consumption; this activation task has no matched baseline and is not a savings measurement.</p>'+a(r.report_path,'Native acceptance receipt')+' · '+a(r.stream_path,'Complete native response stream')+'<details><summary>Native launch and actual tools</summary>'+pre(r.command)+pre(r.tool_names)+'</details><details><summary>Complete returned answer, selected native results and lifetime stats</summary>'+pre(r.final_answer)+pre(r.retained_native_results)+pre(r.direct_context_stats||'No stats requested in this focused corrective attempt.')+'</details></td></tr>').join('')):'<p class="empty">Fresh client task receipt has not been imported.</p>';
  const clientSummary=table(['Native workflow','Accepted checks and correction lineage','Actual consumption'],aggregate.map(x=>'<tr><td><strong>'+e(x.client)+'</strong><p>'+pill(x.passed?'Functional adoption accepted':'Unresolved failure',!x.passed)+'</p></td><td>'+checks(x.checks)+'<details><summary>Each check, source attempt and retained failures</summary>'+pre(x.lineage)+pre(x.original_failures_retained)+'</details></td><td><strong>'+n(x.total_tokens_consumed)+' tokens consumed</strong><p class="small">Original plus focused correction. No matched baseline; zero savings credit assigned.</p>'+pre(x.usage_by_attempt)+'</td></tr>').join(''))+'<p>Both clients first received two invalid fixture targets: an external file and a source outside Serena’s configured Bash scope. One focused follow-up per client used valid existing project inputs. Original failures and all attempt costs remain below.</p>';
  $('adoption').insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin','<h2>Installed native workflow</h2><p>'+e(installation.claim)+'</p>'+installed+'<details><summary>Upstream setup and scope</summary>'+pre(installation.install_commands)+installation.upstream_sources.map(p=>a(p,'Pinned upstream source')).join(' · ')+pre(installation.limitations)+'</details><h2>Useful tasks in Claude and Codex</h2>'+clientSummary+clients);
  $('overview').insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin','<div class="note"><strong>'+profiles.filter(p=>p.passed).length+' / '+profiles.length+' client profiles have upstream RTK awareness installed.</strong> Action-first startup instructions are saved. '+aggregate.filter(r=>r.passed).length+' / '+aggregate.length+' native client workflows accepted across the retained attempts. <p><button id="open-adoption">View installation and task results</button></p></div>');
  $('open-adoption').onclick=event=>{event.preventDefault();showTab('adoption');};
}
$("research-baselines").innerHTML=study?'<p>'+e(study.claim)+'</p>'+table(['Provider / task','Full context','Focused context','Observed difference','Quality acceptance'],study.comparisons.map(p=>'<tr><td>'+e(p.provider)+' / '+e(p.task)+'</td><td>'+n(p.full_total)+'</td><td>'+n(p.focused_total)+'</td><td>'+n(p.full_minus_focused_tokens)+' fewer ('+n(p.full_minus_focused_percent)+'%)</td><td>'+pill(p.both_semantic_pass?'Both semantic grades passed':'Semantic failure',!p.both_semantic_pass)+pill(p.both_protocol_pass?'Both protocol checks passed':'Full answer failed word protocol',!p.both_protocol_pass)+'<p class="small">Semantic score '+n(p.full_semantic_score)+' → '+n(p.focused_semantic_score)+'</p></td></tr>').join(''))+'<details class="native"><summary>Native commands, source and limitations</summary>'+pre(study.native_commands)+pre(study.limitations)+a(extra.native_study.artifact.path,'Captured study receipt')+'</details>':'<p class="empty">No additional native study imported.</p>';
const retrieval=extra.retrieval_evaluation?.result;
const choices=extra.native_choices?.result;
if(choices){
  const choiceRows=(choices.comparisons||[]).map(p=>'<tr><td><strong>'+e(p.component)+'</strong><p>'+e(p.task||p.id)+'</p></td><td>'+n(p.baseline_tokens)+' → '+n(p.candidate_tokens)+'<p class="small">Candidate versus original</p></td><td><strong>'+e(p.selected_format)+'</strong><p>'+n(p.selected_artifact.tokens)+' tokens retained; '+n(p.selected_tokens_removed)+' fewer than original</p>'+pill(p.shared_acceptance.passed?'Shared checks passed':'Shared checks failed',!p.shared_acceptance.passed)+'</td><td>'+a(p.baseline_artifact.path,'Original')+' · '+a(p.candidate_artifact.path,'Candidate')+' · '+a(p.selected_artifact.path,'Selected result')+'<details><summary>Quality checks and exact source identity</summary>'+pre(p)+'</details></td></tr>').join('');
  const choiceTable='<h2>Measured native output choices</h2><p>Use the representation that preserves the task requirements at the smaller measured size. Keeping the original records zero improvement. These are four fixed artifact choices, with no new provider savings claim; earlier expansions remain in the evidence.</p>'+table(['Tool / task','Original → candidate tokens','Adopted choice','Evidence'],choiceRows);
  $('adoption').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',choiceTable);
  $('evidence').insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin',choiceTable+'<details class="native"><summary>Native choice commands and complete returned output</summary>'+(choices.operations||[]).map(o=>'<h3>'+e(o.id)+'</h3>'+pre({argv:o.argv,cwd:o.cwd,exit_code:o.exit_code,kind:o.kind})+pre(o.stdout_text)+pre(o.stderr_text)+a(o.receipt_path,'Exact command receipt')).join('')+'</details>');
}
$("retrieval-baseline").innerHTML=retrieval?'<h3>'+n(retrieval.exact_path_audit_summary?.queries_with_gold_at_3)+' / '+n(retrieval.query_count)+' intended sources in the first three results</h3><p>'+n(retrieval.exact_path_audit_summary?.queries_without_gold_at_3)+' misses retained. Frozen QMD lexical queries; source retrieval quality does not establish answer accuracy or net token savings.</p><details><summary>Native benchmark, exact-path audit and scoring limits</summary>'+pre(retrieval.native_summary)+pre(retrieval.exact_path_audit_summary)+pre(retrieval.limitations)+a(extra.retrieval_evaluation.artifact.path,'Complete captured benchmark')+'</details>':'<p class="empty">No retrieval-quality benchmark imported.</p>';
const hook=D.hook_inventory||{};
$("hook-inventory").innerHTML=table(['Client / enabled state','Configured hooks','Observed retained sources','RTK adoption'],(hook.runtimes||[]).map(r=>'<tr><td><strong>'+e(r.runtime)+'</strong><p>'+pill(r.context_mode_enabled&&r.hook_engine_enabled?'Context Mode enabled':'Enable state incomplete',!(r.context_mode_enabled&&r.hook_engine_enabled))+'</p><span class="small">'+e(r.observed_at)+'</span></td><td>'+e(r.configured_hooks.join(', '))+'<p class="small">Configured hooks without matching retained source labels: '+e(r.unobserved_hooks.join(', ')||'None')+'</p></td><td>'+Object.entries(r.observed_hook_sources).map(([k,v])=>e(k)+': '+n(v.events)).join('<br>')+'<p class="small">'+n(r.retained_events)+' retained events; '+r.databases.length+' databases</p><details><summary>Dates, exact query and source evidence</summary>'+pre(r)+'</details></td><td>'+e(r.rtk_lane)+'</td></tr>').join(''))+'<div class="note warn">Source labels prove retained observations, not every complete hook path. Missing labels can reflect retention or how startup records are labeled. '+e(hook.prior_scope)+'</div><p>'+a(hook.artifact?.path,'Fresh read-only hook inventory')+' · '+a(hook.prior_acceptance,'Dated task-level hook acceptance')+'</p>';
$("project-counters").innerHTML=table(['Native working directory','Retained input → output','Estimated saved','Known interval / returned command'],(D.project_counters||[]).map(r=>'<tr><td>'+e(r.project_path||'Unattributed')+'<p class="small">'+n(r.events)+' recorded commands</p></td><td>'+n(r.input_tokens)+' → '+n(r.output_tokens)+'</td><td><strong>'+n(r.estimated_saved)+'</strong></td><td>'+e(r.first_event)+'<br>'+e(r.last_event)+'<p>'+e(r.command_status)+'</p>'+(r.native_command?'<details><summary>Direct upstream command and returned result</summary>'+pre({argv:r.native_command.argv,cwd:r.native_command.cwd,exit_code:r.native_command.exit_code})+pre(r.native_command.stdout_text)+pre(r.native_command.stderr_text)+'</details>':'')+'</td></tr>').join(''));
const catalogGroups={};repoMatrix.forEach(r=>catalogGroups[r.classification]=(catalogGroups[r.classification]||0)+1);
$("adoption-totals").innerHTML='<p>'+Object.entries(catalogGroups).map(([k,v])=>pill(n(v)+' '+k,k!=='Selected stack')).join(' ')+'</p><p>'+matrix.filter(c=>c.native_lifetime_kind==='retained estimate').length+' components expose an estimated savings-history report. Every selected component and every catalog repository has an explicit baseline and lifetime availability field.</p>';
const counts={};coverage.forEach(c=>counts[c.status]=(counts[c.status]||0)+1);
$("coverage-summary").innerHTML="<p>"+Object.entries(counts).map(([k,v])=>pill(v+" "+k)).join(" ")+"</p><p>"+(D.gaps?e(D.gaps.components.map(x=>x.id+": "+x.status).join(" · ")):"Gap-repair receipt has not been captured yet.")+"</p>"+(D.issues.length?'<div class="note warn">'+e(D.issues.join("\n"))+"</div>":"");
function nativeBlock(title,command,stdout,stderr,meta){return '<details class="native"><summary>'+e(title)+'</summary>'+pre(command)+(stdout!==undefined?"<h3>Returned stdout</h3>"+pre(stdout):"")+(stderr?"<h3>Returned stderr</h3>"+pre(stderr):"")+"<details><summary>Scope, source and hashes</summary>"+pre(meta)+"</details></details>";}
let native=D.commands.map((r,i)=>nativeBlock(r.argv.map(x=>x.split("/").pop()).join(" ")+" · exit "+r.exit_code,r.argv,r.stdout_text,r.stderr_text,r)).join("");
if(D.context_direct){const c=D.context_direct;native+=nativeBlock("Context Mode · direct ctx_stats({}) output",{tool:c.tool,arguments:c.arguments},c.result.content.filter(x=>x.type==="text").map(x=>x.text).join("\n"),"",{captured_at:c.captured_at,runtime:c.runtime,scope:c.scope_note});}
native+=D.native.filter(v=>v.tool==="context-mode"||!v.latest.success).map(v=>{const r=v.latest_success;return nativeBlock(v.tool+" · "+v.scope+(v.latest.success?"":" · latest refresh FAILED"),r?.evidence.argv||r?.evidence.access||"Native persisted state",r?JSON.stringify(r.metrics.raw,null,2):"No successful source available","",{latest:v.latest,latest_success:r,counter_decreased:v.counter_decreased,snapshots:v.snapshot_count});}).join("");
$("native-results").innerHTML=native;
function life(c){if(c.id==="rtk")return "Retained-history native estimate; project views overlap global.";if(c.id==="context-mode")return "Native session-byte and retained-event estimates, separately scoped.";if(c.id==="headroom")return "Native ledger; lifetime field capped at30days.";if(c.id==="toon")return "No native lifetime/history counter; --stats is per conversion.";return "No upstream savings counter verified for this component. Role-specific E2E evidence below.";}
function toolRender(){const q=$("tool-search").value.toLowerCase(),list=matrix.filter(c=>JSON.stringify([c.id,c.repository,c.role,c.profile,c.version,c.adoption_status,c.native_lifetime_kind,c.baseline_status]).toLowerCase().includes(q));$("tool-count").textContent=list.length+" of "+matrix.length;$("tool-rows").innerHTML=list.map(c=>{const measured=D.comparisons.filter(p=>p.tool===c.id);return '<tr><td><strong>'+a(c.repository,c.id)+'</strong><br><code>'+e(c.version)+'</code><p class="small">'+e(c.role)+'</p>'+pill(c.profile)+'</td><td>'+pill(c.adoption_status)+'<p>'+e(c.adoption_scope)+'</p>'+(c.latest_pass?pill('Original audit: '+c.latest_pass.status,/fail|error|blocked|skip/i.test(c.latest_pass.status))+'<p class="small">'+e(c.latest_pass.scope)+'</p>':'<p class="small">Earlier evidence; no additional functional run imported.</p>')+'<details><summary>'+n(c.passed_operations)+' passed / '+n(c.failed_operations)+' failed recorded operations</summary>'+ops.filter(o=>o.components?.includes(c.id)).map(o=>'<p>'+e(o.id)+' · exit '+e(o.exit_code)+' · '+a(o.receipt_path||o.stdout?.path,'evidence')+'</p>').join('')+'</details></td><td>'+pill(c.native_lifetime_kind,c.native_lifetime_kind!=='retained estimate')+(c.native_command?pre(c.native_command):'')+(c.native_reports||[]).map(r=>'<p><strong>'+n(r.latest_success?.metrics.saved)+'</strong> estimated tokens<br>'+e(r.scope)+(r.latest.success?'':' · latest refresh FAILED')+'</p>').join('')+'<p class="small">'+e(c.lifetime_boundary)+'</p></td><td><strong>'+e(c.baseline_status)+'</strong><p>'+measured.map(p=>n(p.baseline.tokens)+' → '+n(p.candidate.tokens)+' = <strong>'+n(p.tokens_removed)+'</strong> tokens<br>').join('')+'</p>' +(choices?.comparisons||[]).filter(p=>p.component===c.id).map(p=>'<p><strong>Selected workflow: '+e(p.selected_format)+'</strong><br>'+n(p.baseline_tokens)+' → '+n(p.selected_artifact.tokens)+' tokens; '+n(p.selected_tokens_removed)+' fewer. '+a(p.selected_artifact.path,'Accepted selected output')+'</p>').join('')+'<p class="small">Exact causal lifetime provider saving: unknown.</p></td><td>'+e(c.hook_status)+'<details><summary>Upstream adoption commands</summary>'+pre(c.upstream_commands)+'</details><details><summary>'+n((c.canonical_receipts||[]).length)+' canonical acceptance receipts</summary>'+(c.canonical_receipts||[]).map(r=>'<p>'+a(roots.publication+'/'+r.path,r.id)+' · '+e(r.kind)+'</p><p>'+e(r.claim)+'</p>'+pre(r.limitations)).join('')+'</details></td></tr>';}).join('')||'<tr><td colspan="5" class="empty">No matching component.</td></tr>';}
$("tools-intro").textContent=coverage.length+" selected components, including TOON and Context Mode. Counter availability is separate from functional acceptance. Components without savings counters remain useful without an invented lifetime number.";
$("support-runtimes").innerHTML='<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Runtime / installation</th><th>Classification</th><th>Evidence boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+(roots.supporting_inventory||[]).map(r=>'<tr><td>'+e(r.name)+'</td><td>'+e(r.classification)+'</td><td>'+e(r.scope)+'<details><summary>Source or command</summary>'+pre(r)+'</details></td></tr>').join('')+'</tbody></table></div>';
function catalogRender(){const q=$("catalog-search").value.toLowerCase(),list=repoMatrix.filter(r=>JSON.stringify(r).toLowerCase().includes(q));$("catalog-count").textContent=list.length+" of "+repoMatrix.length;$("catalog-rows").innerHTML=list.map(r=>'<tr><td>'+a(r.repository,r.repository.replace('https://github.com/',''))+'</td><td>'+pill(r.classification,r.classification!=='Selected stack')+'<p>'+e(r.execution_status)+'</p><strong>'+e(r.native_lifetime_kind)+'</strong><p class="small">'+e(r.baseline_status)+'; exact lifetime provider saving unknown.</p></td><td><details><summary>'+r.references.length+' typed source reference(s)</summary>'+r.references.map(x=>'<p>'+a(roots.publication+'/'+x.path,x.path)+'<br><code>'+e(x.pointer)+'</code><br>'+e(x.decision||x.disposition||x.kind)+'</p>').join('')+'</details></td></tr>').join('')||'<tr><td colspan="3" class="empty">No matching repository.</td></tr>';}
$("catalog-summary").textContent=rows.length+" unique identities · "+D.catalog.counts.public_star_repositories+" public stars · "+D.catalog.counts.beyond_public_stars+" beyond stars. Source review, adoption and execution are different evidence levels. The catalog does not claim every repository is installed or saves tokens.";
$("comparison-table").innerHTML='<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Tool / boundary</th><th>Baseline</th><th>Candidate</th><th>Exact tokens removed</th><th>Raw evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+D.comparisons.map(p=>"<tr><td><strong>"+e(p.tool)+"</strong><p class=\"small\">"+e(p.boundary)+"</p></td><td>"+n(p.baseline.tokens)+"</td><td>"+n(p.candidate.tokens)+"</td><td>"+n(p.tokens_removed)+"</td><td>"+a(p.baseline.path,"baseline")+" · "+a(p.candidate.path,"candidate")+"<details><summary>Hashes and tokenizer</summary>"+pre(p)+"</details></td></tr>").join("")+"</tbody></table></div>";
$("headroom-fixtures").innerHTML=pre(D.audit.headroom.fixtures.map(x=>({fixture:x.name,before:x.tokens_before,accepted_after:x.tokens_after,tokens_removed:x.tokens_saved,checks_passed:x.pass})))+"<p>Exact compact-request serialization from the local offline guard. Native Headroom event ledger is separate.</p>";
if(extra.fresh_e2e){const f=extra.fresh_e2e.result;$("comparison-table").insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend','<details class="native"><summary>Fresh comparisons: shared acceptance gates and limitations</summary>'+f.comparisons.map(p=>'<h3>'+e(p.component)+' · '+n(p.baseline_tokens)+' → '+n(p.candidate_tokens)+'</h3>'+pre({shared_acceptance:p.shared_acceptance,limitations:p.limitations,baseline:p.baseline_artifact.path,candidate:p.candidate_artifact.path})).join('')+'</details>');$("coverage-summary").insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin','<div class="note"><strong>Fresh pass: '+n(f.operations.length)+' operations across '+n(f.components.filter(c=>c.operation_ids.length).length)+' components.</strong> '+n(f.operations.filter(o=>o.passed).length)+' accepted checks; '+n(f.operations.filter(o=>!o.passed).length)+' failed attempts retained. '+n(f.comparisons.length)+' same-source comparisons; provider inference calls: '+n(f.model_calls)+'.</div><details class="native"><summary>Fresh pass exclusions and quality checks</summary>'+pre(f.unexecuted_boundaries)+pre(f.quality_gates)+a(extra.fresh_e2e.artifact.path,'Complete immutable fresh-pass receipt')+'</details>');}
function operationRender(){const q=$("operation-search").value.toLowerCase(),list=ops.filter(o=>JSON.stringify([o.id,o.components,o.argv,o.purpose,o.passed]).toLowerCase().includes(q));$("operation-count").textContent=list.length+" of "+ops.length;$("operation-results").innerHTML=list.map(o=>'<details class="native"><summary>'+pill(o.passed?"Expected check passed":"Failed / bounded result",!o.passed)+" "+e(o.id)+" · stdout "+n(o.stdout?.tokens)+" tokens</summary><p>"+e(o.purpose||o.scope)+"</p>"+pre({argv:o.argv,cwd:o.cwd,environment_overrides:o.environment_overrides,exit_code:o.exit_code})+"<p>"+a(o.stdout?.path,"Complete stdout")+" · "+a(o.stderr?.path,"Complete stderr")+" · "+a(o.receipt_path,"receipt")+"</p><p class=\"small\">Preview only; exact byte/token counts refer to complete files.</p>"+pre(o.stdout_preview||"Use raw-output link.")+"<details><summary>Counts, hashes and check details</summary>"+pre(o)+"</details></details>").join("")||'<p class="empty">No matching operation.</p>';}
$("provider-evidence").innerHTML=D.audit.provider_runs.map(r=>nativeBlock(r.client+" / "+r.variant+" · accepted "+r.full_acceptance,r.command,JSON.stringify(r.native_usage,null,2),"",{report:r.report_path,evidence:r.evidence,workflow:r.workflow_checks})).join("");
$("practice-content").innerHTML='<div class="grid"><div class="box"><h3>Refresh from native sources</h3>'+pre(D.setup.refresh_command)+'<p>Runs native RTK, Headroom and TOON commands; reads separately scoped upstream Context Mode snapshots. A direct MCP ctx_stats response can be supplied with --context-stats-file after capture.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>Use one useful evidence lane</h3><p>QMD for scoped documents; rg/Serena/ast-grep for focused code; SocratiCode for conceptual retrieval; Context Mode for large output; TOON for suitable JSON; RTK for supported commands. Preserve raw failures and original artifacts.</p></div></div><p>'+e(D.setup.native_hooks)+"</p><p>"+e(D.setup.history)+"</p><p>"+e(D.setup.artifact_history)+"</p><p>PC-wide routing: native Codex, Desktop WSL and native Claude instruction files link the same on-demand guide. Existing scopes and account settings remain separate.</p><p>"+a(roots.practice_guide,"PC practice guide")+" · "+a(D.database,"Persistent local ledger")+" · "+a(roots.output_json,"Complete JSON manifest")+"</p>";
$("public-links").innerHTML=a(roots.publication+"/docs/token-practice.md","GitHub/public practice source")+" · "+a(roots.publication+"/adoption/manifest.json","New-PC adoption entry")+" · "+a(roots.catalog_index,"Canonical grand catalog")+(roots.public_pull_request?" · "+a(roots.public_pull_request,"Reviewed GitHub draft PR"):"");
$("config-details").innerHTML=pre({configuration:roots,issues:D.issues,scope:D.scope});
$("export").onclick=()=>{const u=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([JSON.stringify(D,null,2)],{type:"application/json"}));const x=document.createElement("a");x.href=u;x.download="native-token-lifetime-manifest.json";x.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(u),1000);};
$("tool-search").oninput=toolRender;$("catalog-search").oninput=catalogRender;$("operation-search").oninput=operationRender;
toolRender();catalogRender();operationRender();const initial=location.hash.slice(1);if(document.getElementById(initial)?.classList.contains("panel"))showTab(initial);
window.reportReady={components:coverage.length,repositories:rows.length,operations:ops.length,comparisons:D.comparisons.length,native_scopes:D.native.length,provider_pairs:D.audit.provider_pairs.length};
</script><script>__RETURNED_RESULTS_JS__</script></body></html>
